# Asset licensing

Two different licenses apply to the assets in this repository, and only one of them comes from
upstream.

## 1. Upstream "Better End" assets (MIT)

The original mod ("Better End", <https://github.com/quiqueck/BetterEnd>) states its license as
`MIT (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for some Assets)`. Its `LICENSE` file puts everything in the repository
under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 paulevsGitch, except the files listed in upstream's
`LICENSE.ASSETS`.

Assets taken from upstream keep that MIT license. They are redistributed here with the upstream
copyright notice preserved, which is what the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file in this repository does.

## 2. The CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 assets are deliberately excluded

Upstream's `LICENSE.ASSETS` lists exactly three files under **CC BY-NC-SA 4.0**, with the
attribution "Team BetterX":

| Upstream path | SHA-256 |
|---|---|
| `src/main/resources/assets/betterend/textures/gui/infusion.png` | `7DF6D46943CAD8E58ABB524A2BB0BDD1E3E9B5E43EC089C353F008DAC16AD216` |
| `src/main/resources/assets/betterend/icon_updater.png` | `DC4D55E13E7129285B94A8164A39CBF74AF577CBC38098A59B2764CA05B1C705` |
| `src/main/resources/assets/betterend/lang/de_de.json` | `F823FBC5274F5870BD716792515BA7B45863D4A0B8E23C4A228C7AD352EF9495` |

**None of these three files is present in this repository, in the bundled CraftEngine pack, or in
the built plugin jar.** The exclusion was verified by hashing every file in the project and
comparing the digests against the three above: zero matches. Re-running the check after any future
asset import is recommended:

```powershell
$restricted = @(
  '7DF6D46943CAD8E58ABB524A2BB0BDD1E3E9B5E43EC089C353F008DAC16AD216',
  'DC4D55E13E7129285B94A8164A39CBF74AF577CBC38098A59B2764CA05B1C705',
  'F823FBC5274F5870BD716792515BA7B45863D4A0B8E23C4A228C7AD352EF9495'
)
Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File | Where-Object {
  $restricted -contains (Get-FileHash $_.FullName -Algorithm SHA256).Hash
}
```

Because the CC BY-NC-SA material is non-commercial and share-alike, it is not relicensable under
this repository's MIT terms, so it was not carried over. Nothing in this port needs those files:
the infusion GUI texture belongs to a GUI-driven infusion ritual that is not ported yet, the
updater icon belongs to the mod's auto-updater, and the German translation was replaced by the
port's own CraftEngine language files.

## 3. What is bundled instead

* `plugin/src/main/resources/craftengine/betterend/resourcepack/assets/betterend/textures/`
  -- 906 PNGs. 873 of them are byte-identical to upstream mod textures (MIT); the remaining 33 were
  drawn or adjusted for this port.
* `.../resourcepack/assets/betterend/models/` -- block and item models, most of them rewritten for
  CraftEngine's model system. 915 of the 1614 files in the bundled pack are byte-identical to
  upstream mod assets, all of them MIT-licensed.
* CraftEngine configuration YAML, the biome datapack JSON, the port's Java code and its language
  files are written for this port.

If you are an upstream contributor and would like an asset removed from this repository, open an
issue at <https://github.com/IOVEYOUMC0/BetterEnd-Plugin/issues>.
